ire-FINAL.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"88\",\"title\":\"The Carolingian Dynasty (751-987) and Its Impact on Later Medieval ...\",\"description\":\"843: Treaty of Verdun partitions the Carolingian Empire into three parts for each son. 870: Treaty of Mersen further divides Carolingian Empire, after ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.dbu.edu/mitchell/medieval-resources/carolingian_overview.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"89\",\"title\":\"The End of the Carolingians | Western Civilization - Lumen Learning\",\"description\":\"Following the death of Louis the Pious (Charlemagne's son), the surviving adult Carolingians fought a three-year civil war ending only in the Treaty of Verdun, ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/atd-herkimer-westerncivilization/chapter/the-end-of-the-carolingians/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"90\",\"title\":\"Reading: The High Middle Ages – The Birth of Europe Fall 2022\",\"description\":\"During the rest of the ninth and tenth centuries, however, the invasions of the Magyars, Saracens, and Vikings had undermined the stability of the fragile ...\",\"url\":\"https://pressbooks.cuny.edu/thebirthofeuropefall2022/chapter/chapter-1-the-high-middle-ages/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"91\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Mohammedan, Viking, and Magyar Attacks on Europe\",\"description\":\"For four centuries many regions suffered devastating invasions and attack, and unlike the earlier Germanic migrations, which were gradual and involved ...\",\"url\":\"https://heritage-history.com/site/hclass/catholic_knowledge/saints_heroes/kingdoms/vikings.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"92\",\"title\":\"The Viking Raid on Lindisfarne | English Heritage\",\"description\":\"In 793, Vikings destroyed the church at Lindisfarne, a sacred site, with plunder and slaughter, sending a shockwave through Europe.\",\"url\":\"https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/lindisfarne-priory/History/viking-raid/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"93\",\"title\":\"Your guide to the Viking raid of Lindisfarne in AD 793 - HistoryExtra\",\"description\":\"Jun 1, 2019 · On June 8, AD 793, a surprise Viking raid occurred at Lindisfarne, a religious community, marking the start of Viking conquest and expansion.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyextra.com/period/viking/guide-viking-raid-lindisfarne-what-happened-when/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"94\",\"title\":\"The Great Heathen Army - Historic UK\",\"description\":\"In 865, a sizeable Viking force – estimated to be around some 3,000 men – landed on the Isle of Thanet in Kent with the intention of seizing England…\",\"url\":\"https://www.historic-uk.com/HistoryUK/HistoryofEngland/Great-Heathen-Army/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"95\",\"title\":\"The Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte: How the Vikings became Normans\",\"description\":\"Jan 8, 2025 · In 911, Rollo, a Viking chieftain, was granted the title of Duke of Normandy, marking the beginning of Norman rule. · The treaty granted Rollo ...\",\"url\":\"https://thevikingherald.com/article/the-treaty-of-saint-clair-sur-epte-how-the-vikings-became-normans/1093\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"96\",\"title\":\"The Lindisfarne Raid That Began the Viking Age - Life in Norway\",\"description\":\"Jul 13, 2025 · The northmen's unexpected, vicious attack on the monastery at Lindisfarne in 793 is widely regarded as the beginning of the Viking Age.\",\"url\":\"https://www.lifeinnorway.net/lindisfarne-viking-raid/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"97\",\"title\":\"Hungarian Conquests Of Europe - About History\",\"description\":\"The Hungarian conquests in Europe were carried out in the 9th and 10th centuries ... In 899, the Magyars defeated the army of the King of Italy Berengar II in a ...Missing:  key | Show results with:key\",\"url\":\"https://about-history.com/hungarian-conquests-of-europe/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"98\",\"title\":\"The Battle of Lechfeld 955 AD - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"Dec 20, 2020 · Marauding Magyar warriors cross the Lech R