annica.com/event/Battle-of-Manzikert\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"Urban II: Speech at Clermont - Internet History Sourcebooks Project\",\"description\":\"In 1094 or 1095, Alexios I Komnenos, the Byzantine emperor, sent to the pope, Urban II, and asked for aid from the west against the Seljuq Turks, ...Missing:  plea | Show results with:plea\",\"url\":\"https://sourcebooks.web.fordham.edu/source/urban2-5vers.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"Urban II: Speech at Council of Clermont (1095) - The Latin Library\",\"description\":\"I hoped to find you as faithful and as zealous in the service of God as I had supposed you to be. But if there is in you any deformity or crookedness contrary ...Missing:  Byzantine plea\",\"url\":\"https://www.thelatinlibrary.com/imperialism/readings/urban.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"Revisiting the Crusades: Defense, Faith, and Survival\",\"description\":\"Aug 25, 2024 · Islamic Expansion and Christian Response. For centuries, Islam showed it would continue to expand and to subjugate or eradicate other ...\",\"url\":\"https://historymedieval.com/revisiting-the-crusades-defense-faith-and-survival/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"The Crusades: A Very Brief History, 1095-1500 - Medievalists.net\",\"description\":\"Mar 7, 2025 · These expeditions were conducted primarily to defend the Holy Places against Muslim attempts at reconquest or, following its loss in 1187 and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.medievalists.net/2025/03/crusades-history-1095-1500/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://historyguild.org/the-curious-creation-of-the-crusader-states/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"The Crusades: Consequences \u0026 Effects - World History Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Oct 9, 2018 · The power of the royal houses of Europe and the centralisation of government increased thanks to an increase in taxes, the acquisition of wealth ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/article/1273/the-crusades-consequences--effects/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"Effects of the Crusades | Overview, Results \u0026 Significance - Study.com\",\"description\":\"Learn about the effects of the Crusades related to increased commerce, the spread of ideas to Europe, political change, and religious reform in Europe.\",\"url\":\"https://study.com/academy/lesson/results-and-impact-of-the-crusades.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"Timeline of the Crusades - Historic UK\",\"description\":\"Jul 16, 2023 · 23 June 1218 – 5 November 1219 – Siege of Damietta results in Crusaders successfully taking the city. The plan is to use the city as a critical ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historic-uk.com/HistoryUK/HistoryofEngland/Timeline-Crusades/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"Major Crusades and their outcomes - The Middle Ages - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"Disunity among Crusader states weakens their ability to defend against Muslim attacks · Lack of consistent support from European powers leaves Crusader states ...\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/the-middle-ages/unit-8/major-crusades-outcomes/study-guide/SE5MUJ58C4KPJyfe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Impact of Holy Land Crusades on State Formation - Lisa Blaydes\",\"description\":\"While Byzantine and Iberian Christians were engaged in battle with Muslims on their own soil, other Europeans mobilized for war without concern for territorial ...\",\"url\":\"https://blaydes.people.stanford.edu/sites/g/files/sbiybj24621/files/media/file/blaydes_crusades.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"Scholastic Philosophy: The Classical Method for Attaining Wisdom ...\",\"description\":\"May 1, 2025 · Key figures in the theological development of Scholasticism include: St. Anselm of Canterbury (1033–1109): Often called the “Father of ...\",\"url\":\"https://classicalliberalarts.