-the-hundred-years-war-between-england-and-france-research-paper\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"195\",\"title\":\"The Economic Impact of the Black Death – EH.net\",\"description\":\"Less vital labor services were commuted for cash payments and ad hoc wage labor then hired to fill gaps. ... serfs. The Black Death may indeed have made its ...\",\"url\":\"https://eh.net/encyclopedia/the-economic-impact-of-the-black-death/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"196\",\"title\":\"The Economic Impact of the Black Death\",\"description\":\"The Black Death was the largest demographic shock in European history. We review ... serfdom in western Europe, a decline in the authority of religious ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/jel.20201639\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"197\",\"title\":\"How the Black Death made life better | Department of History\",\"description\":\"Jun 18, 2021 · Farm work was peasant work, whether performed by serfs bound to a particular manor, tenant farmers or wage laborers hired by the year or the ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.wustl.edu/news/how-black-death-made-life-better\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"198\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Economic Impact of the Black Death\",\"description\":\"Aug 4, 2020 · DIRECT ECONOMIC EFFECTS IN THE LONG RUN. We now consider how the plague shaped Europe's economies in the long-run. The definition of the long ...\",\"url\":\"https://www2.gwu.edu/~iiep/assets/docs/papers/2020WP/JedwabIIEP2020-14.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"199\",\"title\":\"Social and Economic Effects of the Plague - Brown University\",\"description\":\"Because of illness and death workers became exceedingly scarce, so even peasants felt the effects of the new rise in wages. The demand for people to work the ...\",\"url\":\"https://webhelper.brown.edu/decameron/plague/effects/social.php\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"200\",\"title\":\"Medieval Banking- Twelfth and Thirteenth Centuries | OSU eHistory\",\"description\":\"By the end of the thirteenth century, with its economic resurgence, three classes of credit agents became distinguishable: the pawnbroker, the moneychangers and ...\",\"url\":\"https://ehistory.osu.edu/articles/medieval-banking-twelfth-and-thirteenth-centuries\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"201\",\"title\":\"The economy | The Later Middle Ages - Oxford Academic\",\"description\":\"Were the late Middle Ages a period of commercial contraction, depression, or expansion? Did the economically most significant changes occur in the trade of high ...\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/book/39318/chapter/350575657\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"202\",\"title\":\"Did the Hundred Years War against France strengthen a sense of ...\",\"description\":\"Initially, the conflict was not so much a national war between England and France as a dynastic conflict between two monarchs over a particular territory.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.ox.ac.uk/did-hundred-years-war-against-france-strengthen-sense-english-national-identity\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"203\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyskills.com/classroom/year-8/hundred-years-war-reading/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"204\",\"title\":\"Exploring the 100 Years' War: Causes, Key Battles, and Impact\",\"description\":\"Nov 6, 2024 · The 100 Years' War was a defining conflict in the history of Europe, shaped by a mix of dynastic ambition, territorial disputes, and emerging national ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cliffsnotes.com/study-notes/22605776\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"205\",\"title\":\"Causes of the Wars of the Roses - World History Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Feb 12, 2020 · The Wars of the Roses (1455-1487 CE) was a series of dynastic conflicts between the monarchy and the nobility of England.Missing:  consolidation | Show results with:consolidation\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/article/1498/causes-of-the-wars-of-the-roses/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"206\",\"title\":\"How did the Wars of the Roses shape the ... - TutorChase\",\"description\":\"The Wars of the Roses significantly shaped the English Parliament by consolidating royal authority and paving the way for a more centralised government.\",\"url\":\"https://www.tutorchase.com/answers/a-level/history/how-did-the-wars-of-the-roses-shape-the-development-of-the-english\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"207\",\"title\":\"Ferdinand and Isabella: The Marriage That Unified Spain\",\"description\":\"May 31, 2022 · The Kingdom of Spain charts its origin in the marriage of Ferdinand and Isabella in 1469. Their union, and their rule, triggered a war that forged the modern ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/marriage-of-ferdinand-and-isabella/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"208\",\"title\":\"The Reconquista | Western Civilization - Lumen Learning\",\"description\":\"Around 1480, Ferdinand II of Aragon and Isabella I of Castile, known as the Catholic Monarchs, established what would be known as the Spanish Inquisition. It ...Key Points · Terms · Spanish Inquisition\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/atd-herkimer-westerncivilization/chapter/the-reconquista/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"209\",\"title\":\"Habsburg rule - (AP European History) - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"Habsburg rule significantly shaped the political landscape by using strategic marriages to consolidate power and expand territories across Europe. This approach ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/key-terms/ap-euro/habsburg-rule\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"210\",\"title\":\"European Civilization, 1648-1945: Lecture 2 Transcript\",\"description\":\"Now, we have a process in late Medieval Europe of the consolidation of territorial monarchies. You did have monarchies like Spain, England, and France, namely. ...\",\"url\":\"https://openmedia.yale.edu/projects/iphone/departments/hist/hist202/transcript02.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"211\",\"title\":\"The Avignon Papacy's Ecclesiastical Reforms - The Faithful Historian\",\"description\":\"Nov 26, 2023 · Instances of corruption, indulgences, simony, and even immorality among clergy members were on the rise. This state of affairs deeply troubled ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thefaithfulhistorian.com/p/avignon-papacys-ecclesiastical-reforms\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"212\",\"title\":\"What was the Avignon Papacy? - World History Edu\",\"description\":\"Jan 27, 2025 · The papacy's perceived corruption and French domination damaged its reputation, weakened its spiritual authority, and fueled calls for reform. A ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://worldhistoryedu.com/what-was-the-avignon-papacy/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"History 102: Western Civilization (II) The Crisis of Papal Monarchy\",\"description\":\"The Great Schism intensified more general criticisms of church power in the West. There had been critics of corruption in the church and the monarchy of popes ...\",\"url\":\"https://pages.uoregon.edu/dluebke/Reformations441/Conciliarism.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"(PDF) The Great Western Schism Himanshi S - Academia.edu\",\"description\":\"The Great Western Schism (1378-1417) caused a significant division within the Roman Catholic Church, primarily driven by political disputes rather than ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/7086344/The_Great_Western_Schism_Himanshi_S\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"Renaissance diplomacy: Compromise as a solution to conflict - Diplo\",\"description\":\"This period marked the first long peaceful period after a century of wars. Peace lasted until 1494 when Italy was invaded by France. The Peace of Lodi codified ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.diplomacy.edu/histories/renaissance-diplomacy-compromise-as-a-solution-to-conflict/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"Council of Constance 1414-18 - Papal Encyclicals\",\"description\":\"The Council of Constance aimed to end the church schism, eradicate heresies, and reform church morals. It was summoned by John XXIII and Emperor Sigismund.Missing:  movement | Show results with:movement\",\"url\":\"https://www.papalencyclicals.net/councils/ecum16.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"What was the conciliar movement / conciliarism? | GotQuestions.org\",\"description\":\"Jun 16, 2023 · The Council of Constance (1414–1418) deposed two of the existing popes (the third abdicated) and elected Martin V as the sole pope. That ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.gotquestions.org/conciliar-conciliarism.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"title\":\"John Wycliffe condemned as a heretic | History Today\",\"description\":\"May 5, 2015 · He said that there was no scriptural justification for the papacy's existence and attacked the riches and power that popes and the Church as a ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historytoday.com/archive/john-wycliffe-condemned-heretic\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"219\",\"title\":\"John Wycliffe: The Morning Star of the Reformation\",\"description\":\"Oct 20, 2021 · Wycliffe rejected papal supremacy. He did not believe that the bishop of Rome was infallible or had supremacy over other bishops or should have ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.logos.com/grow/john-wycliffe-morning-star/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"220\",\"title\":\"Jan Hus (1369-1415) and the Hussite wars (1419-1436)\",\"description\":\"Hus was a Czech priest, who, a century before Luther, called for a reform of the Chuch and was burnt at the stake. His death set off a religious, political and ...\",\"url\":\"https://museeprotestant.org/en/notice/jan-hus-1369-1415-and-the-hussite-wars-1419-1436/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"221\",\"title\":\"Bohemian Reformation - World History Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Nov 17, 2021 · Jan Hus was the central figure of the Bohemian Reformation as it was his martyrdom in 1415 that radicalized the movement and led directly to the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/Bohemian_Reformation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"222\",\"title\":\"Petrarch | Biography, Renaissance, Humanism, Sonnets, Poems ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 16, 2025 · Petrarch (born July 20, 1304, Arezzo, Tuscany [Italy]—died July 18/19, 1374, Arquà, near Padua, Carrara) was an Italian scholar, poet, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Petrarch\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"223\",\"title\":\"Petrarch | The Poetry Foundation\",\"description\":\"His poetry, mainly composed sonnets focusing on the intense love and admiration he has for Laura, became immensely popular, and in 1341 he was crowned the poet ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/petrarch\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"224\",\"title\":\"William of Ockham - Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy\",\"description\":\"Sep 11, 2024 · He is probably best known today for his espousal of metaphysical nominalism. Indeed, the principle known as “Ockham's Razor” is named after him.\",\"url\":\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/ockham/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"225\",\"title\":\"William of Ockham: Pioneering Nominalism and Empiricism\",\"description\":\"Dec 14, 2023 · By advocating for nominalism, Ockham rejected the scholastic reliance on abstract, metaphysical entities and placed greater emphasis on the ...William of Ockham: Context... · Application of Ockham's Razor...\",\"url\":\"https://philosophy.institute/ancient-medieval/william-of-ockham-nominalism-empiricism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"226\",\"title\":\"Dante and The Divine Comedy: He took us on a tour of Hell - BBC\",\"description\":\"Jun 5, 2018 · Writing in the vernacular, and helping to create a new vernacular for much of Italy, allowed Dante's ideas to take wide root – and helped set ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20180604-dante-and-the-divine-comedy-he-took-us-on-a-tour-of-hell\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"227\",\"title\":\"14.3 Dante and the emergence of vernacular literature - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"Dante Alighieri revolutionized literature by writing in Italian vernacular. His masterpiece, the Divine Comedy, proved complex ideas could be expressed in ...\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/the-middle-ages/unit-14/dante-emergence-vernacular-literature/study-guide/j4y56nT90tl9LKL4\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"228\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Giovanni-Boccaccio/The-Decameron\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"229\",\"title\":\"Guide to the Classics: Boccaccio's Decameron, a masterpiece of ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 11, 2020 · Written between 1348 and 1353, the Decameron is a prescription for psychological survival, a way of mentally distancing from today's death ...\",\"url\":\"https://theconversation.com/guide-to-the-classics-boccaccios-decameron-a-masterpiece-of-plague-and-resilience-143437\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"230\",\"title\":\"How the Black Death Radically Changed the Course of History - GEN\",\"description\":\"Apr 1, 2020 · In 1352, the Black Death petered out, having killed a third of Europe. But the pestilence was not finished. It returned five times before the ...\",\"url\":\"https://gen.medium.com/how-the-black-death-radically-changed-the-course-of-history-644386f5b803\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"231\",\"title\":\"How universities helped transform the medieval world | CEPR\",\"description\":\"May 21, 2012 · To identify universities' causal effect, we exploit a 'natural experiment' in university establishment: the Papal Schism of the 14th century.Missing:  15th | Show results with:15th\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/how-universities-helped-transform-medieval-world\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"232\",\"title\":\"The rise of universities and scholasticism - The Middle Ages - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"14th-15th centuries saw further growth and diversification of universities. Establishment of universities in various European cities (Prague, Vienna, Heidelberg) ...\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/the-middle-ages/unit-10/rise-universities-scholasticism/study-guide/xHzFbvoSQKtOYHwC\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"233\",\"title\":\"Full article: The impact of the Black Death on medieval universities ...\",\"description\":\"The Black Death has been seen as a turning point in European history,Footnote as it caused many changes in the economic, technological, social, demographic, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00309230.2025.2538198?src=\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"234\",\"title\":\"The Black Death and industrialisation: Lessons for today's South\",\"description\":\"Jun 4, 2014 · The Black Death led to an improvement in agricultural technology, changed the status of women, and increased wages. This process helped the Industrial ...\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/black-death-and-industrialisation-lessons-todays-south\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"235\",\"title\":\"The Black Death and the Great Transition - Medievalists.net\",\"description\":\"Aug 7, 2021 · Manorialism never recovered. With land plentiful, wages high, and fewer limits on social and geographical mobility, serfdom all but disappeared.\",\"url\":\"https://www.medievalists.net/2021/08/the-black-death-and-the-great-transition/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"236\",\"title\":\"10 Medieval Inventions that Changed the World - Medievalists.net\",\"description\":\"Jun 29, 2023 · 1. Mechanical Clock · 2. Printing Press · 3. Gunpowder · 4. Water and Wind Mills · 5. Coffee House · 6. Eyeglasses · 7. Public Library · 8. Flying ...Missing:  1300-1500 | Show results with:1300-1500\",\"url\":\"https://www.medievalists.net/2023/06/medieval-inventions-world/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"237\",\"title\":\"18 Inventions that shaped Europe in the Middle Ages\",\"description\":\"Mar 3, 2023 · 1. The printing press was a revolutionary medieval invention · 2. The coffee house was ahead of its time · 3. The heavy plow led to the ...\",\"url\":\"https://interestingengineering.com/lists/18-inventions-of-the-middle-ages-that-changed-the-world\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"238\",\"title\":\"Medieval Civil and Military Technological Inventions and Innovations\",\"description\":\"Nov 16, 2023 · The period saw major technological advances, including the adoption of gunpowder, the invention of vertical windmills, spectacles, mechanical clocks, and ...\",\"url\":\"https://brewminate.com/an-analysis-of-medieval-civil-and-military-technological-inventions-and-innovations/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"239\",\"title\":\"Does the Fourteenth-Century Black Death Hold Lessons for Today's ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 27, 2020 · In turn, the scarcity of labor inspired a wave of labor-saving new technologies—vessels that could sail farther with smaller crews, soon ...\",\"url\":\"https://epicenter.wcfia.harvard.edu/blog/does-fourteenth-century-black-death-hold-lessons-todays-pandemic\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"240\",\"title\":\"Inventions Timeline: Middle Ages Innovations - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"May 5, 2025 · Invention Highlights During the Middle Ages · Movable Type Printing Press · Magnetic Compass · Buttons for Clothing · Numbering System · Gun.Missing:  600-1000 | Show results with:600-1000\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/middle-ages-timeline-1992478\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"241\",\"title\":\"Government - Feudalism, Monarchy, Church - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Oct 9, 2025 · Various institutions had emerged to fill the gap. The Christian church, against enormous odds, had kept the light of religion and learning ...Missing:  enduring | Show results with:enduring\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/government/The-Middle-Ages\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"242\",\"title\":\"Academic Market and The Rise of Universities in Medieval and Early ...\",\"description\":\"The study argues that the integration of an academic market enabled universities to operate together, generating knowledge and potentially paving the way for ...\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/jeea/article/22/4/1541/7438871\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"243\",\"title\":\"Medieval Learning: Universities \u0026 Philosophy | The Middle Ages ...\",\"description\":\"The liberal arts curriculum of the medieval universities had a lasting impact on Western education and helped to shape the idea of a well-rounded education ...Structure And Curriculum · Major Thinkers And Their... · Scholasticism And Debate\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/the-middle-ages/unit-10\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"244\",\"title\":\"The Medieval Law School - UC Berkeley Law\",\"description\":\"The medieval law school began in Bologna with Roman law, then spread to other universities, focusing on civil and canon law, and students formed guilds.\",\"url\":\"https://www.law.berkeley.edu/research/the-robbins-collection/exhibitions/medieval-law-school/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"245\",\"title\":\"Magna Carta: Muse and Mentor Interpreting the Rule of Law\",\"description\":\"Magna Carta was interpreted as a permanent charter of individual liberties, a safeguard against arbitrary royal action, and a declaration of rights held since ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.loc.gov/exhibits/magna-carta-muse-and-mentor/interpreting-the-rule-of-law.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"246\",\"title\":\"Magna Carta and contemporary constitutional change\",\"description\":\"Magna Carta has since taken on legendary status in England, the UK and globally as a symbol of democracy and the rule of law. In particular, chapters 39 and 40 ...\",\"url\":\"https://historyandpolicy.org/policy-papers/papers/magna-carta-and-contemporary-constitutional-change/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"247\",\"title\":\"16.1 The decline of feudalism and the rise of centralized states\",\"description\":\"This shift towards centralized authority reshaped the political landscape of medieval Europe, setting the stage for modern nation-states.Missing:  evolution | Show results with:evolution\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/the-middle-ages/unit-16/decline-feudalism-rise-centralized-states/study-guide/QeCfQj7CRu4oHlj3\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"248\",\"title\":\"Transformation of European States: From Feudal to Modern\",\"description\":\"Formation of modern states in Europe demonstrates a conspicuous feature of stage-by-stage development during the transition from feudalism to capitalism.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S187704281001147X\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"249\",\"title\":\"Medicine and Society in the Medieval Hospital - PMC\",\"description\":\"At the end of the early Middle Ages, the Benedictine monks revived the hospital institution. Hospitals flourished in the crusades, with the rise of orders ...\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2359880/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"250\",\"title\":\"History of Hospitals - Penn Nursing - University of Pennsylvania\",\"description\":\"Religious orders of men predominated in medieval nursing, in both Western and Eastern institutions. [2] The Alexian Brothers in Germany and the Low ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nursing.upenn.edu/nhhc/nurses-institutions-caring/history-of-hospitals/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"251\",\"title\":\"The charity and the care: the origin and the evolution of hospitals\",\"description\":\"Hospitals originated in early Christian age, initially in the bishop's house, then monasteries, and finally autonomous buildings, supported by donations.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0953620512002890\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"252\",\"title\":\"Christianity's Role in the Development of Modern Institutions\",\"description\":\"Christianity influenced modern institutions by adapting Roman structures, creating universities, influencing parliaments, and developing welfare, medical, and ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.wesleyan.edu/christianitystudies/pathways/development.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"253\",\"title\":\"The Myth of the 'Dark Ages' Ignores How Classical Traditions ...\",\"description\":\"May 18, 2023 · The Myth of the 'Dark Ages' Ignores How Classical Traditions Flourished Around the World. The author of a sweeping re-examination of Western ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/the-myth-of-the-dark-ages-ignores-how-classical-traditions-flourished-around-the-world-180982190/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"254\",\"title\":\"The Great Myths 15: What about \\\"the Dark Ages?\\\" - History for Atheists\",\"description\":\"Sep 29, 2024 · But the Middle Ages also saw the invention or development of technologies such as blast furnaces, mechanical clocks, astronomical clocks, ...\",\"url\":\"https://historyforatheists.com/2024/09/the-great-myths-15-what-about-the-dark-ages/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"255\",\"title\":\"Science Was Alive and Well in the Dark Ages | Discover Magazine\",\"description\":\"Jan 29, 2021 · Another common misconception is that scientific progress largely went dark during this era, snuffed out by the medieval church. But if you ask ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.discovermagazine.com/science-was-alive-and-well-in-the-dark-ages-42197\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"256\",\"title\":\"There's no such thing as the 'Dark Ages', but OK - Going Medieval\",\"description\":\"May 26, 2017 · There is, quite literally, observably, and extensively proven no “dent” made to “scientific thinking” in the medieval period. Manuscripts also ...\",\"url\":\"https://going-medieval.com/2017/05/26/theres-no-such-thing-as-the-dark-ages-but-ok/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"257\",\"title\":\"4 Stupid Stories About the Middle Ages Everyone Tells\",\"description\":\"Jun 27, 2024 · The story that grinds my gears is the idea that the medieval period was devoid of scientific and technological progress. Contrary to popular ...\",\"url\":\"https://irpathak.medium.com/4-stupid-stories-about-the-middle-ages-everyone-tells-1cb348d094cf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"258\",\"title\":\"Why did science make little real progress in Europe in the Middle ...\",\"description\":\"This question is based on the common but erroneous belief that there was no scientific progress in the Middle Ages.\",\"url\":\"https://www.quora.com/Why-did-science-make-little-real-progress-in-Europe-in-the-Middle-Ages-3\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"259\",\"title\":\"Population Estimates - Internet History Sourcebooks Project\",\"description\":\"Population Estimates 500-1500AD ... It is very difficult to know even the approxmate population of various parts of Europe during the Middle Ages. Yet such ...\",\"url\":\"https://sourcebooks.web.fordham.edu/source/europe-populationetstimates500-1500.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"260\",\"title\":\"The Commercial Revolution of the Middle Ages, 950–1350\",\"description\":\"The Commercial Revolution of the Middle Ages, 950–1350. Search within full text.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/commercial-revolution-of-the-middle-ages-9501350/27C2AF7F2C913BADCDC29631B71EA7BF\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[{\"id\":\"d7eff29778ee\",\"caption\":\"Europe at the onset of the Middle Ages\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Europe_and_the_Near_East_at_476_AD.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"d7eff29778ee\",\"caption\":\"Europe and the Near East at 476 AD\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Europe_and_the_Near_East_at_476_AD.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"97d5f880b543\",\"caption\":\"Early medieval village\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Fr%C3%BChmittelalterliches_Dorf.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"ff39d0c4a514\",\"caption\":\"Map of the expansion of the Caliphate\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Map_of_expansion_of_Caliphate.svg.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"9367941d3579\",\"caption\":\"Frankish Empire expansion\",\"url\":\"._assets_/Frankish_Empire_481_to